## The core finding

This guide is drawn at **0.088 m/pt** (store 659: 0.118), so its shopping aisles are only ~12.9 pt (~1.1 m) wide. The auto-derived service disks (r=130 pt, bridge=12 pt) therefore **bridged real shopping aisles shut** — the Toys/Seasonal runs, the whole Kitchen housewares block (that was the `unreachable_shelf_labels` cluster at (1156,365): Calderos/Cookware/Dinnerware/Flatware/Beverage/Foil), and the Card & Party aisles. Two of the derived disks had no counter to seal at all: `KITCHEN` here is a **housewares department** (Calphalon, Appliances, Cookware), and `FLORAL` is an **open display island**. The derived checkstand rect also ran 60 pt too far north, eating the Seasonal bin floor.

The three counters that genuinely are staff-only are all drawn as **walled rooms**, so I traced them verbatim instead of relying on bridging.

## Files authored (`data/94/`)

- **`exclusions.json`** — 3 polys traced from the PDF strokes: the deli/bakery service enclosure, the seafood counter + prep area behind it, the pharmacy room behind the counter. Each swallows its own department label, which is what retires the `BAKERY`/`SEAFOOD`/`PHARMACY` VERIFYs.
- **`seal_zones.json`** — full override, one zone: the checkstand lane bank `[516,596,832,678]` bridge 14 (lanes are 6–9 pt gaps). All derived disks dropped, with the reasoning recorded in the entry's `name`.
- **`inclusions.json`** — the four VERIFY judgment calls, all **legitimate customer space**: the Kitchen housewares floor + its gondola aisles, the Deli east walkway (the red `DELI` label is printed on the open floor, not behind a counter), the north cross-aisle in front of the Deli Meats case, and the 18 pt band in front of the Market Deli wall case.
- **`walk_truth.json`** — 15 `must` / 11 `must_not`; all 26 verified against the built grid.
- `zones.json` not needed — ENTRANCE and CHECKSTANDS labels both extract, so zones derive correctly.

